Copyright (c) 2019-present undefined development
License: MIT (package.json "license": "MIT"; full text below)

HighAsCG's Visuals Flow node library (WO-1011) follows the logic of cables.gl ops (src/ops/base/Ops.*). The ops
were re-implemented in GDScript, per frame with a time step; no cables.gl source file is copied verbatim:

  godot/client/features/visuals/flow_eval.gd    ← Ops.Anim.LFO_v4, Ops.Anim.Smooth, Ops.Anim.Spring,
                                                   Ops.Math.MapRange, Ops.Math.SchlickBias, Ops.Math.Ease,
                                                   Ops.Trigger.Threshold, Ops.Trigger.TriggerCounterLoop,
                                                   Ops.Trigger.NthTrigger, Ops.Trigger.ProbabilityTrigger,
                                                   Ops.Math.TriggerRandomNumber, Ops.Boolean.MonoFlop,
                                                   Ops.Boolean.ToggleBool, Ops.Boolean.And / Or,
                                                   Ops.Number.SwitchNumber, Ops.Number.GateNumber,
                                                   Ops.Number.FreezeNumber, Ops.Number.DelayNumberSimple,
                                                   Ops.Math.SimpleMovingAverage, Ops.Math.Speed,
                                                   Ops.Math.MaxSinceReset
  godot/client/features/visuals/flow_nodes.gd   ← the op set, port and parameter naming of the ops above
  godot/client/features/visuals/flow_presets.gd ← HighAsCG's own patches, built from the nodes above
  godot/client/features/visuals/visuals_flow.gd ← the categorised op browser idea

cables.gl's Ops.Math.PerlinNoise_v3 derives from p5.js (LGPL) and was NOT ported; the Flow "Noise" node is HighAsCG's
own value noise on the LFO hash. The cables.gl name and logo are not used for the feature.

